WEBVTT

00:46.171 --> 00:47.464
Do you want to sleep over?

00:50.633 --> 00:54.137
This is why we had to break up.

00:54.220 --> 00:55.847
NOVEMBER, 2008

00:56.890 --> 00:58.516
Yeon-su, let's go to the cafeteria.

00:58.600 --> 01:01.269
Sorry. I'm not hungry right now.

01:01.352 --> 01:05.315
- Come on. I'll buy you banana milk.
- No, I'm really fine.

01:05.398 --> 01:07.275
- You can go with the others.
- Okay.

01:07.358 --> 01:09.360
Ji-yeon, hurry up. Let's go.

01:10.445 --> 01:11.529
Bye.

01:11.613 --> 01:13.156
Hurry up.

01:13.239 --> 01:15.116
She said no again, right? Why bother?

01:15.200 --> 01:16.576
Stop asking. She can hear you.

01:16.659 --> 01:18.787
Hey, you should stop caring about her.

01:18.870 --> 01:21.915
She doesn't care about us.
She's so self-centered.

01:21.998 --> 01:25.835
She's right.
Yeon-su never treated us to anything.

01:25.919 --> 01:27.295
We always bought her stuff.

01:27.378 --> 01:30.590
But still, it wasn't like
she asked us to buy her those things.

01:30.673 --> 01:34.010
But she's shameless
for accepting them every single time.

01:34.677 --> 01:38.014
Remember last time?
You always gave her a birthday gift.

01:38.097 --> 01:40.058
I hate being poor

01:40.642 --> 01:43.228
because I can't be generous to others.

01:46.689 --> 01:48.983
Our family's been poor since I was born.

01:49.067 --> 01:50.151
I didn't do it.

01:50.235 --> 01:51.694
I didn't do it either.

01:51.778 --> 01:53.613
Whatever. Don't worry about it.

01:53.696 --> 01:58.076
It made hanging out with my friends
more and more uncomfortable.

02:01.663 --> 02:04.874
As a young girl, I was quite hurt.

02:06.835 --> 02:08.336
But it was okay.

02:10.004 --> 02:11.131
Grandma.

02:13.424 --> 02:16.928
You're here again. I told you not to come.

02:17.011 --> 02:19.514
It was boring being home alone.

02:19.597 --> 02:20.640
Good grief.

02:20.723 --> 02:23.810
It was okay because I had
something precious to protect.

02:23.893 --> 02:26.396
- Your hands are freezing.
- What about dinner?

02:26.479 --> 02:28.148
Were you busy today?

02:28.231 --> 02:30.233
No, not at all.

02:30.316 --> 02:31.359
Hey, look at her skirt.

02:31.442 --> 02:33.820
- She's obviously a teacher's pet.
- Hey, look at her shoes.

02:33.903 --> 02:35.405
Even my mom wouldn't wear that.

02:35.488 --> 02:37.699
That's why I decided to act nonchalantly

02:37.782 --> 02:39.242
and be self-centered.

02:39.325 --> 02:40.952
Spring is finally here.

02:41.035 --> 02:45.039
- That made things much easier.
- The weather is pretty cold.

02:45.123 --> 02:48.418
I'd like to extend my gratitude
to all those who gathered

02:48.501 --> 02:51.129
to congratulate
and encourage the freshmen.

02:52.130 --> 02:54.007
Hey. What are you looking at?

02:55.091 --> 02:56.426
Thirty-four years ago,

02:57.176 --> 03:01.264
- I was standing where you were…
- That is, until I met Choi Ung.

03:02.682 --> 03:03.683
I'm going to…

03:05.560 --> 03:08.605
I'm going to kill you
if you tell the others that we're dating.

03:10.315 --> 03:12.275
And you better not bother me either.

03:12.358 --> 03:14.068
Studying always come first.

03:14.944 --> 03:17.572
And you need to study hard too
and get into university.

03:24.495 --> 03:26.247
Is there anything you'd like to say?

03:32.170 --> 03:33.504
What are you doing tomorrow?

03:41.804 --> 03:44.807
The only person who has allowed me

03:44.891 --> 03:46.434
to escape from reality

03:47.310 --> 03:48.228
was Ung.

03:52.941 --> 03:54.734
- Did you sleep well?
- Yes.

03:55.401 --> 03:58.112
- Were you waiting long?
- No. I just came.

04:01.115 --> 04:04.035
- So they're both symbolic.
- Okay.

04:04.118 --> 04:06.454
The difference is…

04:06.537 --> 04:09.123
And thus, the population…

04:11.251 --> 04:13.336
Gosh, why am I so sleepy today?

04:17.298 --> 04:19.092
"Since the 1960s…"

04:20.260 --> 04:22.679
- "The rapid industrialization…"
- "Caused…"

04:23.930 --> 04:25.598
2012 ADMISSION RESULT

04:34.941 --> 04:36.985
CONGRATULATIONS

04:37.068 --> 04:38.820
NAME: CHOI UNG
MAJOR: ART AND DESIGN

04:50.873 --> 04:51.749
LET'S GO OUTSIDE

05:12.979 --> 05:14.647
LET'S GO OUTSIDE

05:26.159 --> 05:27.201
Yeon-su.

05:28.703 --> 05:29.746
What?

05:29.829 --> 05:31.998
- Are you already eating something?
- Gimbap.

05:32.081 --> 05:34.500
Darn it. I brought some food for you.

05:36.711 --> 05:39.380
This is kimchi fried rice,
and these are tomatoes.

05:39.464 --> 05:40.631
Did you really make this?

05:40.715 --> 05:43.217
You bet. It's not that hard.

05:49.974 --> 05:52.560
- Is it not good?
- It is.

05:53.895 --> 05:54.979
I agree.

05:59.275 --> 06:01.110
What are you talking about?

06:04.155 --> 06:05.698
When did I act all excited?

06:05.782 --> 06:09.077
You were so excited
that the girls were being flirty with you.

06:09.160 --> 06:11.329
Tell them to treat you like a senior.

06:12.330 --> 06:13.915
Wait…

06:13.998 --> 06:16.626
I'm actually upset
because you were wasting your time.

06:16.709 --> 06:17.627
I'm sorry.

06:17.710 --> 06:22.632
At times, I was desperate
for some comfort away from reality.

06:23.174 --> 06:24.217
COVER LETTER

06:24.300 --> 06:27.512
And that made me forget about reality.

06:29.639 --> 06:33.643
- Are you done?
- No. I still have a few left.

06:33.726 --> 06:35.228
Do you have to get a job right away?

06:36.145 --> 06:37.396
What do you mean?

06:37.480 --> 06:40.066
I mean, instead of getting
a regular 9-to-5 job,

06:40.149 --> 06:42.568
you could study more
and land a better job.

06:42.652 --> 06:44.779
I have no time for that.

06:44.862 --> 06:47.782
I need to get a job
and become a full-time employee.

06:49.033 --> 06:49.992
And then?

06:53.204 --> 06:56.749
Well, I'm going to save up enough money

06:56.833 --> 06:59.043
so that my grandma
won't have to work anymore.

06:59.127 --> 07:00.586
- That's it?
- What?

07:01.963 --> 07:05.550
I know how you worked part-time,
received scholarships,

07:05.633 --> 07:07.927
and studied diligently.

07:08.594 --> 07:11.848
So I thought you'd eye
for a bigger success than that.

07:18.563 --> 07:20.898
I've always thought that my dream was

07:21.524 --> 07:23.860
to live an average, normal life.

07:26.737 --> 07:28.573
I consider that a success.

07:28.656 --> 07:32.452
Maybe this wasn't what I wanted.

07:32.535 --> 07:34.620
What about you? What'll you do?

07:35.955 --> 07:39.834
Me? I don't really have a plan.

07:40.626 --> 07:44.088
You're good at drawing and enjoy doing it.
You could do that for a living.

07:45.256 --> 07:46.591
Drawing is just going to be a hobby.

07:47.175 --> 07:48.009
You know my dream.

07:48.092 --> 07:51.888
It's to bask in the sun during the day
and to lie underneath a lamp at night.

07:52.555 --> 07:54.307
A stressful life is not for me.

07:56.017 --> 08:00.188
Maybe I never had a choice to begin with.

08:00.271 --> 08:02.398
I like my life as it is.

08:02.482 --> 08:03.774
Next to you and my family.

08:10.406 --> 08:13.534
But when I opened my eyes again…

08:19.499 --> 08:23.794
reality struck me harder than ever before…

08:23.878 --> 08:25.129
Why?

08:26.547 --> 08:28.633
Why do we need to pay the debt instead?

08:30.301 --> 08:31.886
I've never even met

08:32.929 --> 08:36.516
this man who's supposedly my uncle.

08:37.308 --> 08:38.893
Yeon-su…

08:41.187 --> 08:42.480
My puppy.

08:43.773 --> 08:45.233
I wish…

08:48.903 --> 08:51.489
I could only be poor to the point

08:52.448 --> 08:54.200
where I could handle it.

09:17.515 --> 09:19.934
…as if to mock me
for having dared to dream.

09:22.436 --> 09:23.646
Hello?

09:28.401 --> 09:29.318
Yeon-su!

09:29.860 --> 09:31.195
Before I knew it…

09:39.537 --> 09:42.957
reality had me in its grasp.

09:49.338 --> 09:50.590
I won't go.

09:52.800 --> 09:54.885
You know this is
every student's dream, right?

09:56.095 --> 09:58.014
Don't you know that you're talented?

09:58.097 --> 10:00.182
Your skills had improved greatly

10:00.266 --> 10:02.810
when you were gone there for six months.

10:02.893 --> 10:04.478
That's because it was six months.

10:05.146 --> 10:07.732
Living there for a few years is different.

10:07.815 --> 10:10.276
And I don't want to go there
all by myself.

10:10.359 --> 10:11.485
That's your reason?

10:12.862 --> 10:15.072
You can draw all the buildings you love

10:15.156 --> 10:17.325
and learn much more if you go there.

10:19.118 --> 10:21.329
Do you have no ambitions?

10:22.496 --> 10:26.876
No. I'm not interested
in striving for success.

10:27.585 --> 10:30.546
Give this chance to someone
who needs it more than I do.

10:30.630 --> 10:32.006
My gosh.

10:41.223 --> 10:43.559
SEO-YEON UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL
INPATIENT BILL

10:58.699 --> 11:01.285
What? When did you get here?

11:02.078 --> 11:04.288
It's not like you to wait for me.

11:06.040 --> 11:08.084
Should we have lunch? What do you want?

11:08.876 --> 11:10.044
Should we go out?

11:19.804 --> 11:20.971
So…

11:22.056 --> 11:24.183
the reason why we had to break up was…

11:24.725 --> 11:26.936
Why would we break up?

11:30.564 --> 11:32.817
Because we live in
two very different realities.

11:33.526 --> 11:35.945
I'm always the first thing
you abandon when things get tough.

11:36.987 --> 11:40.241
Rather, it was because
my reality was pathetic.

11:40.908 --> 11:43.035
Am I the easiest thing you have

11:44.036 --> 11:45.162
that you can throw away?

11:48.707 --> 11:49.834
No.

11:52.628 --> 11:54.004
You're the only thing

11:54.964 --> 11:56.090
I can throw away.

12:02.054 --> 12:03.431
Why are you doing this?

12:04.181 --> 12:05.307
Actually…

12:07.143 --> 12:11.605
it's because life alone
was too much of a burden for me.

12:11.689 --> 12:13.065
What reason do you have?

12:14.024 --> 12:15.317
To be honest…

12:16.444 --> 12:18.654
Why do we have to break up?

12:20.614 --> 12:23.617
To be completely honest,

12:24.785 --> 12:28.831
I was afraid you'd eventually notice
my inferiority complex.

12:30.166 --> 12:36.964
EPISODE 6
PRIDE AND PREJUDICE

12:52.646 --> 12:55.441
I'm pretty sure
I was working in my studio.

13:31.810 --> 13:34.730
God, you scared me to death!

13:34.813 --> 13:36.482
Don't sneak up on me like that.

13:36.565 --> 13:38.651
- When did you get here?
- Just now.

13:38.734 --> 13:40.903
I thought you'd have trouble
sleeping again.

13:42.154 --> 13:44.448
Go back to sleep.
You probably didn't get enough.

13:44.532 --> 13:46.408
Hey, what time did I go to bed?

13:46.492 --> 13:48.285
How would I know?

13:48.369 --> 13:50.621
My gosh.

13:51.413 --> 13:52.706
How did I sleep so soundly?

13:53.374 --> 13:54.708
I slept so well.

13:54.792 --> 13:57.670
Your stopwatch was stopped
a little after 10 p.m.

13:58.420 --> 14:00.589
- You must have fallen asleep right away.
- Did I?

14:00.673 --> 14:02.967
- Did you take sleeping pills?
- Yes.

14:03.050 --> 14:06.512
Geez. Why did you sleep
on the sofa and not your bed?

14:09.974 --> 14:11.392
What is that?

14:20.109 --> 14:22.778
Ung, you've managed to work for 95 hours.

14:23.362 --> 14:25.364
You must be in your element.

14:25.447 --> 14:26.574
I'm impressed.

14:27.074 --> 14:28.826
Hey. What time did you get here again?

14:28.909 --> 14:30.870
Me? About 7:30 a.m.

14:30.953 --> 14:32.162
Was I alone then?

14:32.246 --> 14:33.455
- No.
- Then?

14:33.539 --> 14:34.915
You've always been alone.

14:34.999 --> 14:36.333
Come on.

14:36.417 --> 14:40.212
Right. Ji-ung is going to stop by
and edit the footage of you working.

14:40.296 --> 14:43.757
Also, he's going to film
the live drawing show.

14:43.841 --> 14:47.344
Let's show him
how awesome you are when you're drawing.

14:47.428 --> 14:49.346
Forget the loser you used to be…

14:51.390 --> 14:52.391
Are you listening?

14:53.225 --> 14:55.269
How long has it been
since I slept this well?

14:55.936 --> 14:58.063
You did? Did you not wake up at all?

14:58.147 --> 15:00.190
- No.
- That's great.

15:00.274 --> 15:02.484
Good. You'll be in great condition today.

15:05.404 --> 15:08.490
Then what is this unsettling feeling?

15:12.328 --> 15:15.164
Why are you up so early on the weekend?

15:15.247 --> 15:18.709
Today's the day of the opening event
that I've been working hard on.

15:18.792 --> 15:20.878
Really? It's today?

15:20.961 --> 15:21.962
- Sit down.
- Okay.

15:22.046 --> 15:24.965
Gosh, time sure does fly.

15:25.049 --> 15:27.635
If you have time later,
drop by later with your friend.

15:27.718 --> 15:30.471
That's okay. I don't want to distract you.

15:30.554 --> 15:32.598
You worked so hard on that project.

15:33.182 --> 15:35.017
I'm sure you did a fantastic job.

15:35.100 --> 15:37.227
You're the only one who appreciates me.

15:39.939 --> 15:42.232
You know what?

15:43.734 --> 15:46.278
The welfare center

15:46.362 --> 15:49.198
is accepting job application forms.

15:49.865 --> 15:51.533
I'm thinking of applying.

15:51.617 --> 15:55.537
What? Don't be ridiculous.

15:55.621 --> 15:57.915
No. You're still unwell.

15:58.582 --> 16:00.709
I'm just bored. That's all.

16:00.793 --> 16:05.047
Staying in this house all day
is really suffocating.

16:05.130 --> 16:08.342
You should hang out
at the senior citizen center.

16:08.425 --> 16:12.012
No, thanks.
There's nothing to do there. It's boring.

16:12.096 --> 16:14.682
They're just a bunch of sick, old people.

16:14.765 --> 16:17.059
You have no friends
because of your temper.

16:17.142 --> 16:20.020
What? You say that
as if I'm the neighborhood bully.

16:20.813 --> 16:23.107
Anyway, I'm just letting you know.

16:23.190 --> 16:26.694
Come on. What if you collapse?

16:26.777 --> 16:27.736
Then I'll…

16:28.862 --> 16:33.117
I'm afraid staying home all day
will make me forgetful.

16:33.784 --> 16:37.705
What's that disease old people get?
Dementia, I think it's called.

16:39.915 --> 16:42.793
I'm just saying. I don't actually have it.

16:42.876 --> 16:46.380
I'm extremely clearheaded for my age.

16:46.463 --> 16:48.882
No one can hold a candle to me.

16:49.550 --> 16:51.844
So don't you worry about a thing.

16:52.720 --> 16:54.096
Eat up.

16:56.015 --> 16:57.391
I'm not worried.

16:58.434 --> 17:02.312
Then why are you staring at me like that
and making me feel embarrassed?

17:02.396 --> 17:04.773
I'm just upset and heartbroken.

17:04.857 --> 17:08.235
You've been working all your life.

17:08.944 --> 17:10.446
Can't you just take it easy?

17:10.529 --> 17:13.699
It doesn't get easier than this.

17:13.782 --> 17:16.118
You cook and prepare my meals.

17:16.201 --> 17:18.203
I'm eating and sleeping well.

17:18.704 --> 17:23.500
Goodness. I am blessed indeed.

17:23.584 --> 17:26.045
Gosh, cut that nonsense and eat up.

17:28.589 --> 17:29.882
Then…

17:31.925 --> 17:33.552
don't do anything too demanding.

17:34.178 --> 17:38.390
If it's just for a few hours a day,
I'll think about it.

17:38.474 --> 17:41.101
You're so ridiculous.

17:41.185 --> 17:45.773
Who do you think you are? My mother?

17:46.523 --> 17:49.651
Of course. I'm your guardian.

17:50.486 --> 17:52.821
You better not cross me.

17:55.199 --> 17:57.117
Look at you.

17:57.201 --> 17:58.494
- Honey, wait.
- Why?

17:58.577 --> 17:59.453
- Ho.
- What?

17:59.536 --> 18:00.871
What are you wearing?

18:00.954 --> 18:02.790
Chang-sik, look. How do I look?

18:02.873 --> 18:04.792
This won't do. Put on the other necktie.

18:04.875 --> 18:06.752
- Why?
- The red one's better.

18:06.835 --> 18:08.629
Have you seen the restaurant owners?

18:08.712 --> 18:10.172
- Ji-ung!
- They're kind-hearted.

18:10.255 --> 18:12.299
I'm glad you're here. Look at us.

18:12.382 --> 18:14.384
How do we look?

18:14.468 --> 18:18.764
You look like you're a couple
from a wealthy neighborhood.

18:18.847 --> 18:20.349
I can barely recognize you guys.

18:22.059 --> 18:25.562
Ung is going to put on a show today.

18:26.146 --> 18:28.607
He's always putting on a show,

18:28.690 --> 18:30.943
so why would you get
all dressed up for that?

18:31.026 --> 18:34.238
Not like that, you fool.
An actual performance.

18:34.321 --> 18:37.741
Ung is going to draw
in front of an audience.

18:37.825 --> 18:41.662
Eun-ho came by last time
and said we had to come.

18:41.745 --> 18:44.164
He never invited us to those things.

18:44.248 --> 18:45.999
But isn't it too early right now?

18:46.083 --> 18:49.086
- Not at all.
- We'll be in the front row.

18:49.169 --> 18:52.172
Oh, dear! Honey, we need
to pick up the rice cakes.

18:52.256 --> 18:55.259
You're right. We need to go early
and give them rice cakes.

18:55.342 --> 18:58.637
Wait. You should hand them out
to just your neighbors

18:58.720 --> 19:00.055
unless you want Ung to faint.

19:00.139 --> 19:03.016
- Still, we should show our courtesy.
- That's right.

19:03.100 --> 19:05.519
- They're going all the way there for him.
- Exactly.

19:05.602 --> 19:09.815
Those people begged him to draw.

19:09.898 --> 19:12.442
It'll all be ready,
and he'll be treated like a king.

19:12.526 --> 19:15.946
Is that true? My goodness! Honey!

19:16.029 --> 19:17.823
Goodness!

19:17.906 --> 19:19.324
Did you hear that?

19:19.408 --> 19:22.369
They begged my son to draw for them.

19:22.452 --> 19:24.371
Is that really why he's drawing?

19:24.454 --> 19:26.498
That's how big he's become.

19:27.166 --> 19:28.709
- I can't believe this.
- Gosh.

19:28.792 --> 19:31.545
Anyway, you don't have to rush.
So take your time.

19:40.971 --> 19:44.308
It's the final day
of our long-term project.

19:44.975 --> 19:46.185
Right.

19:46.268 --> 19:48.353
We should grab something to eat

19:48.437 --> 19:52.733
- before they let the audience in.
- We don't have time.

19:52.816 --> 19:54.735
No. Today will be hectic.

19:54.818 --> 19:56.820
Let's have our last meeting over lunch.

19:56.904 --> 19:58.697
Okay. I'll make the order.

19:58.780 --> 20:01.366
Let me. Do sandwiches sound okay?

20:01.450 --> 20:02.534
- Yes.
- Great.

20:04.119 --> 20:08.081
Well, should I get
the same menu for all of us?

20:08.165 --> 20:09.875
You see, I'm on a diet.

20:09.958 --> 20:12.377
I'd like wheat bread, roast chicken,
olive oil, and pepper.

20:12.461 --> 20:15.923
I'd like steak with no pickles.
I can't eat them.

20:16.006 --> 20:18.550
And for me…
What was that sauce from last time?

20:18.634 --> 20:19.927
I wrote it down somewhere.

20:22.221 --> 20:24.514
- Let me order instead.
- Okay.

20:24.598 --> 20:26.892
You'll have what you normally have, right?

20:26.975 --> 20:28.018
Sure.

20:37.069 --> 20:40.030
Ms. Kook, are you okay?
You look quite tired.

20:40.113 --> 20:41.114
I'm all right.

20:41.907 --> 20:43.200
As you've asked,

20:43.283 --> 20:46.203
we've set two separate press conferences
for Nu-a and Go-oh.

20:46.787 --> 20:48.789
Jean Ferrat will arrive from the airport

20:48.872 --> 20:51.041
around the time the drawing show ends.

20:51.124 --> 20:52.501
Okay. Thank you.

20:53.961 --> 20:56.797
Do you know when Go-oh will arrive?

20:58.590 --> 20:59.800
Do you want to sleep over?

21:15.607 --> 21:16.692
Ms. Kook?

21:18.151 --> 21:20.279
It's okay. I'll ask.

21:20.988 --> 21:21.905
Okay.

21:21.989 --> 21:25.409
Also, Mr. Jang just arrived.
He's on the first floor.

21:25.492 --> 21:26.368
I see.

21:27.286 --> 21:28.328
Aren't you going to see him?

21:28.412 --> 21:29.913
I'll see him once it begins.

21:31.748 --> 21:34.668
Enjoy your meal, and we'll meet
at the front gate in 30 minutes.

21:34.751 --> 21:36.670
I'll take a look around the second floor.

21:36.753 --> 21:37.838
- Okay.
- Okay.

21:40.549 --> 21:43.552
Today's interview will be
about you as an artist.

21:43.635 --> 21:45.554
Feel free to talk about your occupation.

21:45.637 --> 21:46.930
Like what?

21:47.014 --> 21:49.224
Your thoughts about your work,

21:49.308 --> 21:53.478
your life as an artist,
or your future plans and goals.

21:55.981 --> 21:56.857
I don't have any.

21:58.233 --> 21:59.943
Can you ask me a different question?

22:00.610 --> 22:05.324
Then tell me how you began drawing.

22:12.664 --> 22:13.915
There's no story to tell.

22:15.959 --> 22:17.544
Fine. Say that then.

22:17.627 --> 22:19.671
It'll make him look like an airhead.

22:19.755 --> 22:21.673
But that's the truth.

22:21.757 --> 22:23.425
Don't try to sugarcoat anything.

22:24.593 --> 22:25.719
I'll start now.

22:31.141 --> 22:32.309
We're almost there.

22:33.060 --> 22:34.352
Are you not nervous?

22:34.936 --> 22:38.190
- What?
- In a way, this is your debut.

22:39.066 --> 22:41.985
It's your first public appearance.
Are you not nervous?

22:42.069 --> 22:43.862
If I say yes, will you cancel it?

22:43.945 --> 22:45.489
Of course not. Hang in there.

22:46.198 --> 22:49.076
This song has always made you relax.

22:50.410 --> 22:52.079
Play "Island" by NJ.

22:55.207 --> 22:58.668
I'm happy that
you're finally out of your cave.

22:59.252 --> 23:00.462
I was never in one.

23:00.545 --> 23:02.798
You practically were.

23:04.591 --> 23:07.636
To be honest, I was worried sick
that you'd have trouble sleeping

23:07.719 --> 23:11.932
and become anxious since Yeon-su appeared.

23:12.015 --> 23:15.936
But in the end, this is all thanks to her.

23:16.478 --> 23:18.730
You would have never done this
had I asked you to.

23:19.898 --> 23:24.319
Anyway, I hope you'll continue working
with others out in the open.

23:25.278 --> 23:28.281
Then you'll become
even more famous, get a lot of work,

23:28.365 --> 23:29.783
and make lots of money.

23:31.910 --> 23:36.498
That being said, what's your take
on giving your manager a raise?

23:36.581 --> 23:37.707
I'm against it.

23:37.791 --> 23:42.170
I see. Then let's take our time and
discuss that topic further in the future.

23:42.254 --> 23:44.047
- What?
- We're here.

23:48.927 --> 23:50.720
Go to the second floor first.

23:50.804 --> 23:53.890
Your green room will be there.
I'll park and bring your stuff over.

23:53.974 --> 23:56.101
Do you know
how much your welfare expense--

23:56.184 --> 23:59.312
They're honking back there. Go on, now.

24:00.313 --> 24:02.315
- See you later.
- See you soon.

24:35.307 --> 24:37.559
GO-OH, NU-A

24:49.738 --> 24:52.657
GO-OH

25:00.999 --> 25:03.293
We should run it by Ms. Kook.

25:03.960 --> 25:06.463
Mr. Kang, have you seen Ms. Kook?

25:06.546 --> 25:08.632
I saw her heading to the second floor.

25:08.715 --> 25:11.218
I see. Let's check the showroom.

25:49.673 --> 25:52.926
She always looked mad in front of me.

25:57.514 --> 25:58.515
I think

25:59.808 --> 26:01.810
I finally appreciate Yeon-su
for who she is.

26:15.991 --> 26:19.202
We already interviewed Ung.
We just need Yeon-su's now.

26:19.286 --> 26:20.996
Let's get a rough footage first,

26:21.079 --> 26:23.331
then focus on Ung when the show begins.

26:23.415 --> 26:25.625
Intern, stay with her.

26:25.709 --> 26:27.085
Yes, sir. I will.

26:27.168 --> 26:29.045
Should I go interview her?

26:30.422 --> 26:31.506
No, I'll do it.

26:31.589 --> 26:34.718
We have a meeting
back at the office, so let's hurry.

26:34.801 --> 26:35.719
Yes, sir.

26:54.738 --> 26:56.364
Is this the green room?

26:57.574 --> 26:58.408
It's Ung.

26:58.491 --> 26:59.659
Yes.

26:59.743 --> 27:00.994
When did he get here?

27:17.302 --> 27:18.803
What should I say

27:19.846 --> 27:21.598
if he brings up last night?

27:21.681 --> 27:22.849
About yesterday…

27:26.561 --> 27:27.937
Did you visit me?

27:29.481 --> 27:30.690
I knew it.

27:31.524 --> 27:33.443
He doesn't remember.

27:35.653 --> 27:39.491
Yes. I had something to give you
so I went over to your place.

27:40.283 --> 27:41.201
I see.

27:43.870 --> 27:45.830
Then did I--

27:46.581 --> 27:48.958
Sorry. I need to get ready.

27:49.042 --> 27:52.712
The staff will tell you the details
regarding the live show.

27:58.218 --> 28:01.596
But still,
there's no need for me to avoid him.

28:03.348 --> 28:04.265
Hey.

28:06.518 --> 28:07.352
Good luck.

28:08.561 --> 28:09.437
Thanks.

28:23.243 --> 28:24.744
So you didn't run away.

28:24.828 --> 28:26.996
Take a rest, and we'll rehearse later.

28:27.080 --> 28:28.665
Here's the layout and the program.

28:35.922 --> 28:37.340
GO-OH

28:38.550 --> 28:41.094
- Ms. Kook.
- Did you check Go-oh's video?

28:41.177 --> 28:44.389
- Yes, I did. Everything's fine.
- Then play it right now

28:44.472 --> 28:47.142
- with the playlist he's given us.
- Yes, ma'am.

29:21.426 --> 29:22.677
I've never seen

29:23.928 --> 29:25.805
that side of him before.

29:27.724 --> 29:28.767
Ms. Kook.

29:29.267 --> 29:30.435
Ms. Kook.

29:31.352 --> 29:32.562
Ms. Kook.

29:36.858 --> 29:37.859
Ms. Kook.

29:46.868 --> 29:48.328
Ung, we need to head out now.

29:50.622 --> 29:51.664
Are you sleeping?

29:54.209 --> 29:56.669
Are you nervous?
Do you want some more calming pills?

29:57.378 --> 29:58.379
Why did I…

30:00.381 --> 30:01.883
sleep well last night?

30:02.383 --> 30:05.136
How is that a problem?
Are you still hung up on that?

30:05.804 --> 30:07.472
For the caption,

30:08.056 --> 30:11.100
can you write,
"Pondering about what to draw"?

30:12.644 --> 30:13.812
What? Hurry up.

30:13.895 --> 30:15.146
- Not that one.
- Go on.

30:15.230 --> 30:17.065
- No, it's the other one.
- This one? Okay.

30:17.148 --> 30:18.066
Geez.

30:29.202 --> 30:32.455
- I can't see from here.
- Sit down.

30:32.539 --> 30:34.374
Let's go over there.

30:35.250 --> 30:36.251
Nu-a is here.

30:41.756 --> 30:43.424
Hello. It's nice to meet you all.

30:44.008 --> 30:46.845
It's truly an honor to draw the building

30:46.928 --> 30:49.722
designed by my role model, Jean Ferrat.

30:49.806 --> 30:54.143
As you all know, another artist will be
drawing in the next room.

30:54.227 --> 30:55.728
If you're curious, go ahead.

30:56.938 --> 31:01.192
However, I guarantee that
you'll be too captivated to go there.

31:01.276 --> 31:05.405
I'll do my utmost best to win your hearts.
My name is Nu-a,

31:05.488 --> 31:07.699
and I'm an illustrator.

31:12.745 --> 31:13.830
- He's here.
- Hi, Ung.

31:19.085 --> 31:20.503
That's my son.

33:05.942 --> 33:07.735
You've never seen him working, right?

33:08.486 --> 33:09.988
Yes.

33:10.822 --> 33:12.907
I've never seen this side of him before.

33:13.658 --> 33:14.784
I barely recognize him.

33:14.867 --> 33:18.955
He looked like a total stranger
the first time I saw him drawing.

33:19.664 --> 33:20.707
You're right.

33:22.291 --> 33:23.710
Good job, by the way.

33:23.793 --> 33:27.380
This seems like a big event.
It must've been hell preparing for this.

33:27.463 --> 33:29.090
No, it was just part of my job.

33:29.757 --> 33:32.635
But shouldn't you be working
instead of chatting with me?

33:32.719 --> 33:35.638
Exactly. I'm here to pick you up.

33:38.057 --> 33:40.184
You can never judge a book by its cover.

33:40.268 --> 33:43.980
Who knew I'd be working side by side
with the kid who had the lowest grade?

33:44.564 --> 33:46.941
Of course, everything was a nuisance.

33:47.025 --> 33:50.445
As you know,
he and I are very different people.

33:51.112 --> 33:52.780
He's kind of slow.

33:52.864 --> 33:55.450
He should have
shared his progress during the project

33:55.533 --> 33:57.618
to make things more efficient.

33:57.702 --> 33:59.454
But he'd never talk about it.

33:59.537 --> 34:00.830
He always keeps his thoughts to himself.

34:00.913 --> 34:04.000
He was always like that.
I'd ask what was on his mind.

34:04.083 --> 34:06.002
"I don't know. I'm not sure. Nothing."

34:06.085 --> 34:07.587
It was one of these three.

34:08.379 --> 34:10.381
I'm getting annoyed
just thinking about it.

34:11.758 --> 34:12.717
No.

34:13.509 --> 34:14.510
Well…

34:14.594 --> 34:16.054
NOT EVEN ONE?

34:16.137 --> 34:19.057
Seeing him draw like that
for the first time

34:19.140 --> 34:22.226
made me discover a new side to him.

34:23.603 --> 34:25.980
He used to draw back then too,

34:26.064 --> 34:28.733
but he never looked that serious.

34:29.692 --> 34:33.863
I don't know what's gotten into him,
but he's completely focused.

34:33.946 --> 34:35.531
He seems different.

34:36.949 --> 34:41.037
But you know what?
He was always serious about drawing.

34:41.120 --> 34:43.247
I think it was in episode five.

34:43.331 --> 34:45.333
I ruined his drawing once,

34:45.416 --> 34:47.502
and he threw a huge fit.

34:48.419 --> 34:50.463
Honestly, I felt bad about that.

34:50.546 --> 34:54.759
But seeing him
all worked up was entertaining.

34:54.842 --> 34:57.720
He rarely gets upset.

34:58.262 --> 35:01.557
I admit that I teased him
a few more times for fun.

35:05.478 --> 35:07.396
He was so hilarious.

35:15.571 --> 35:16.656
Well…

35:17.490 --> 35:20.076
I've never seen him like that before.

35:21.410 --> 35:24.288
It feels as if he has changed.

35:27.166 --> 35:29.127
I thought he'd never change.

35:35.049 --> 35:38.386
I rambled on, didn't I?
Let's edit that out.

35:39.512 --> 35:41.806
- Next question then.
- Okay.

36:03.327 --> 36:06.622
Shouldn't he take a break?

36:06.706 --> 36:09.584
That is how he always works.

36:09.667 --> 36:12.795
But since there's an audience,
he must feel extremely tense.

36:14.505 --> 36:16.424
Let me check on him.

36:18.676 --> 36:20.428
Honey, let's go.

36:28.519 --> 36:31.480
Goodness. Is that you, Yeon-su?

36:32.064 --> 36:33.065
Hello.

36:33.149 --> 36:35.693
Gosh, it's been ages.

36:35.776 --> 36:37.862
I heard you were
filming the documentary with Ung.

36:37.945 --> 36:40.489
I am. How have you been?

36:40.573 --> 36:42.825
Well, it's always the same for us.

36:43.576 --> 36:47.496
Goodness. You haven't changed at all.

36:47.580 --> 36:49.165
The same goes for you both.

36:49.248 --> 36:51.083
It's because of our outfits.

36:51.167 --> 36:53.377
Are you here to see Ung today?

36:53.461 --> 36:54.670
Yes.

36:54.754 --> 36:56.380
Then why are you leaving already?

36:56.881 --> 36:58.716
It's dragging on, isn't it?

36:58.799 --> 37:00.384
- No.
- Not at all.

37:01.135 --> 37:04.847
Seeing him draw all alone
makes us feel sad.

37:04.931 --> 37:06.807
It reminds me of when he was young.

37:07.433 --> 37:09.936
To think that he's been
doing that since he was little--

37:10.019 --> 37:11.687
- That's enough. Let's go.
- Okay.

37:12.313 --> 37:16.192
I told you to come over for a meal.
What's stopping you?

37:16.275 --> 37:18.319
Don't think too much about it
and just come over.

37:18.402 --> 37:20.279
We won't charge you.

37:21.113 --> 37:22.865
He's right. You should come.

37:22.949 --> 37:24.367
- Come on.
- I'll cook you a delicious meal.

37:24.450 --> 37:26.661
- Okay.
- All right.

37:39.423 --> 37:40.633
Ung…

37:41.884 --> 37:43.427
didn't take the breakup too well.

37:45.429 --> 37:47.223
It must have been hard for you too.

37:54.146 --> 37:56.732
We really want you to visit.

37:56.816 --> 37:58.526
Please do. Okay?

37:58.609 --> 38:00.278
Okay. I will.

38:00.361 --> 38:01.862
All right. Bye.

38:04.115 --> 38:06.742
- Hurry up.
- Coming.

38:06.826 --> 38:07.743
Bye.

38:07.827 --> 38:09.287
Hurry up.

38:48.576 --> 38:49.535
Ji-ung.

38:50.578 --> 38:51.829
Did you do the interview?

38:51.912 --> 38:53.664
Yes. What about the shoot?

38:54.165 --> 38:56.083
There's nothing to film.

38:56.167 --> 38:58.544
He's been sitting there
going at it for hours.

38:58.627 --> 39:02.089
Head back to the office with the intern
and prepare for the meeting.

39:02.173 --> 39:03.799
I'll wrap things up here.

39:08.554 --> 39:12.016
Ung didn't take the breakup too well.

39:19.065 --> 39:20.691
Do you want to sleep over?

39:27.531 --> 39:29.992
Are you sick?

39:46.759 --> 39:48.761
How many pills did you take?

39:49.345 --> 39:50.805
Do you take them often?

39:50.888 --> 39:53.182
Do you? Since when?

39:53.265 --> 39:56.102
Since when did you have trouble sleeping?
Why didn't you tell me?

40:29.093 --> 40:30.094
Yes?

40:31.345 --> 40:33.055
Here you are.

40:33.139 --> 40:35.433
Nu-a is almost done.

40:35.516 --> 40:39.562
Escort him to the first floor
for the press conference when he's done.

40:39.645 --> 40:41.689
I'll escort Go-oh.

40:41.772 --> 40:43.190
Yes, ma'am.

41:00.207 --> 41:01.959
I still have some time left.

41:04.336 --> 41:05.254
Hello.

41:05.754 --> 41:07.131
I'm Go-oh.

41:34.742 --> 41:36.660
Congratulations.

41:38.496 --> 41:40.414
This is a side of you I haven't seen.

41:43.584 --> 41:44.793
Gosh. Is that NJ?

41:55.304 --> 41:57.848
Wait. Excuse me.

41:58.516 --> 41:59.767
Seriously?

42:00.726 --> 42:01.560
NJ!

42:03.187 --> 42:04.647
Gosh.

42:23.374 --> 42:25.084
GO-OH, NU-A

42:25.167 --> 42:26.669
Hello, Ms. Kook.

42:26.752 --> 42:28.462
It must have been a long day.

42:28.546 --> 42:30.422
Thank you so much for your work today.

42:30.506 --> 42:33.801
There's an after-party later,
so feel free to attend.

42:33.884 --> 42:36.345
I'll wrap it up here. You can go first.

42:36.929 --> 42:39.431
Are you sure? We can help.

42:39.515 --> 42:42.685
It's okay.
You had to work on the weekend. Go on.

42:42.768 --> 42:44.728
Are you coming to the after-party?

42:44.812 --> 42:46.897
I'll have to see. Go on.

42:46.981 --> 42:48.899
Goodbye, then.

42:48.983 --> 42:50.901
- See you later.
- You have to come.

43:13.382 --> 43:16.176
Why the hell isn't he picking up?

43:16.802 --> 43:18.304
Ung, over here!

43:18.387 --> 43:20.055
Hey, why weren't you picking up?

43:20.139 --> 43:22.516
Hey, are you done
with the press conference?

43:22.600 --> 43:24.143
Why are you still here?

43:24.226 --> 43:26.228
Well, that was hurtful.

43:26.312 --> 43:28.856
Watch what you say, you ingrate.

43:28.939 --> 43:31.233
She made time to come see you.

43:31.317 --> 43:33.485
Thank you so much for coming.

43:33.569 --> 43:35.237
I didn't expect you to come.

43:35.321 --> 43:37.823
I didn't think I'd come uninvited either.

43:38.574 --> 43:41.493
I arrived late
due to my schedule and took a peek.

43:41.577 --> 43:42.828
You looked different.

43:42.911 --> 43:45.789
I'll make sure to invite you next time.

43:46.498 --> 43:48.500
Right. Let me tell you this

43:48.584 --> 43:51.712
in case you're flustered by your name
being on the trending searches.

43:51.795 --> 43:53.672
I told the reporters that

43:53.756 --> 43:56.925
we're just good friends rooting
for each other, so don't worry.

43:57.593 --> 43:59.595
- Friends?
- Aren't we?

43:59.678 --> 44:02.473
Well, we are.

44:03.349 --> 44:05.726
I'm just flattered
that you considered me a friend.

44:05.809 --> 44:09.271
I've never seen a man
who was happy to be just friends with me.

44:09.355 --> 44:12.358
- Sorry?
- Never mind.

44:12.441 --> 44:14.443
Are you going home? Need a ride?

44:14.526 --> 44:16.070
It's okay. We brought our car--

44:16.153 --> 44:17.488
Okay. Goodbye.

44:17.571 --> 44:20.366
Sorry? Hold on.
Is that why you were waiting for me?

44:20.449 --> 44:23.661
I told you. I'm very busy, but I'm not.

44:23.744 --> 44:25.371
- Goodbye.
- Go home safely.

44:28.707 --> 44:30.000
Goodbye.

44:33.879 --> 44:36.382
Ung, how could you decline her offer?

44:36.465 --> 44:37.925
Shut up. I'm exhausted.

44:38.008 --> 44:40.177
Anyway, you're in trouble now.

44:40.260 --> 44:41.345
What do you mean?

44:41.428 --> 44:43.639
Today, you've finally revealed yourself

44:43.722 --> 44:45.849
and won everyone's hearts.

44:45.933 --> 44:48.310
That's enough. Go get the car.

44:48.936 --> 44:51.772
This means that you've agreed
to give me a raise.

44:51.855 --> 44:53.899
Come on. I said, go.

44:55.567 --> 44:56.944
This was from NJ, right?

44:58.362 --> 44:59.738
It smells different.

45:02.241 --> 45:04.576
Go-oh has finally debuted!

45:19.299 --> 45:20.259
It's sweet.

45:21.635 --> 45:22.803
You're so pathetic.

45:23.595 --> 45:26.723
Why are you **tching around here
on such a good day?

45:26.807 --> 45:29.351
What do you mean?
I came in case you were bored.

45:30.394 --> 45:33.230
You must be the reason why
my business is failing.

45:33.939 --> 45:36.316
You should be at the party

45:36.400 --> 45:40.612
celebrating the end of the project
instead of throwing a pity party here.

45:40.696 --> 45:42.948
- I like this more.
- This is being pathetic.

45:43.031 --> 45:45.826
Aren't you ecstatic
that your hard work paid off?

45:47.077 --> 45:49.830
Not really. It's just work.

45:49.913 --> 45:52.708
Now that we're done,
we'll begin another project.

45:55.252 --> 45:56.587
Is work very tough?

45:57.254 --> 46:00.299
No. Compared to my previous job,
it's actually easier.

46:01.049 --> 46:03.427
It's fine.

46:05.929 --> 46:07.139
Then what's the problem?

46:11.977 --> 46:14.313
It's neither demanding

46:15.522 --> 46:16.899
nor fun.

46:18.984 --> 46:21.361
It's just work.

46:24.615 --> 46:25.782
Have a drink.

46:35.417 --> 46:36.710
Remember what you said?

46:38.170 --> 46:42.132
You said my eyes
looked empty and soulless.

46:43.217 --> 46:44.760
Yes, and it still is.

46:45.344 --> 46:48.305
The fish I have back there
has livelier eyes than you do.

46:49.932 --> 46:54.686
I saw Ung's eyes as he was drawing today.

46:56.355 --> 46:58.982
They seemed so soulful.

47:02.236 --> 47:03.362
He did?

47:03.862 --> 47:04.863
Yes.

47:05.948 --> 47:08.825
He was so focused on his drawing.

47:11.119 --> 47:12.579
To be honest, I was jealous.

47:13.789 --> 47:15.832
Why would you be
jealous of someone like him?

47:17.167 --> 47:18.293
Aren't I pathetic?

47:19.545 --> 47:21.672
I hated pathetic people the most.

47:22.756 --> 47:24.800
While he was changing,

47:25.342 --> 47:30.013
I was busy making ends meet
and haven't changed at all.

47:30.931 --> 47:33.350
Even I think I'm pathetic.

47:33.976 --> 47:35.686
Geez. You're ridiculous.

47:36.228 --> 47:39.815
You weren't stagnant.
Think of the debt you paid off.

47:39.898 --> 47:42.067
I know how hard you worked.

47:42.651 --> 47:45.779
You've succeeded
by coming this far, you wench.

47:48.991 --> 47:51.535
I'm going to celebrate
the ending of the project.

47:51.618 --> 47:53.996
I'll be your VIP customer.
Line up the soju bottles.

47:54.079 --> 47:56.707
- I already put nine on your tab.
- Really?

47:56.790 --> 47:58.208
I'll be ripping you off too.

47:59.751 --> 48:02.838
- Goodness. Hello.
- Hello.

48:03.463 --> 48:04.673
- Hello.
- Over here.

48:04.756 --> 48:05.674
Okay.

48:12.472 --> 48:14.391
- Here's the menu.
- What's today's special?

48:14.474 --> 48:15.934
- It's jjamppong rice.
- I see.

48:16.018 --> 48:17.019
No, it's jjamppong stew.

48:18.979 --> 48:20.939
Ung, good work today.

48:22.733 --> 48:24.443
I'm going home. Rest up.

48:25.444 --> 48:26.445
Okay.

48:27.321 --> 48:30.616
Hey. Turn off that light on your way out.

48:30.699 --> 48:32.868
All right. Bye.

48:32.951 --> 48:34.036
Bye.

49:02.439 --> 49:04.399
- Here's your food.
- That looks good.

49:04.483 --> 49:06.276
- I'll take the empty bottles.
- Okay.

49:07.110 --> 49:09.696
Hey, you're here.
Sorry for calling out of the blue.

49:09.780 --> 49:12.324
As you know, I'm the only friend she has.

49:12.407 --> 49:15.577
But I'm too busy tonight
to get rid of her myself.

49:15.661 --> 49:18.038
I can't hand her over
to the police either.

49:18.121 --> 49:21.458
She'll be upset when she wakes up,
but what can I do? Please help me out.

49:21.541 --> 49:22.542
Take her away.

49:23.293 --> 49:25.545
Coming. One minute.

49:42.938 --> 49:44.106
Ung?

49:57.953 --> 49:59.830
God, that's cold.

50:03.792 --> 50:04.876
Are you awake?

50:05.877 --> 50:06.878
Yes.

50:11.425 --> 50:12.801
Didn't you get any sleep?

50:12.884 --> 50:13.969
Yes.

50:15.345 --> 50:17.139
On top of that, I drank.

50:17.222 --> 50:18.598
I think I'm drunk.

50:18.682 --> 50:19.725
Drink this.

50:19.808 --> 50:21.768
How considerate of you.

50:29.067 --> 50:32.154
Sorry you had to come here at this hour.
It must have been a hassle.

50:32.237 --> 50:35.323
Not really.
I was at a boring get-together.

50:35.991 --> 50:38.034
- Did you drink too?
- A bit.

50:38.118 --> 50:39.745
But you're a lightweight.

50:40.579 --> 50:42.873
- You remember that?
- Of course.

50:42.956 --> 50:45.167
It surprised me
how little you could drink.

50:46.376 --> 50:47.544
That was harsh.

50:55.635 --> 50:58.847
By the way, how is the documentary going?

50:59.639 --> 51:00.974
It's going okay.

51:01.057 --> 51:04.144
I don't think
I should have agreed to do it.

51:04.770 --> 51:07.731
Back in high school,
we were at least young and cute.

51:07.814 --> 51:09.983
But all you can film now is me working.

51:10.066 --> 51:11.485
Of course, it'll be boring.

51:12.444 --> 51:14.780
I'm afraid this documentary
is going to be a flop.

51:14.863 --> 51:16.239
Maybe you want it to fail.

51:16.323 --> 51:18.533
I actually do.
I'll make sure no one watches it.

51:18.617 --> 51:20.577
You know I'm good at PR.

51:20.660 --> 51:21.995
I'm going to spread a rumor.

51:27.334 --> 51:30.086
But I'll think twice
if you agree to let me watch it first.

51:31.797 --> 51:34.299
- Watch it first?
- I may have looked ugly

51:34.382 --> 51:36.927
or blurted out obscenities accidentally.

51:37.010 --> 51:40.180
And I'm certain Ung bad-mouthed me.

51:41.139 --> 51:44.184
Anyway, I am curious.

51:49.314 --> 51:53.735
By the way, what did Ung say about me?

52:01.201 --> 52:02.202
I mean…

52:03.203 --> 52:04.830
- Did he bad-mouth--
- Do you…

52:07.582 --> 52:09.167
still like Ung?

52:23.515 --> 52:26.393
Do you still like Ung?

52:28.061 --> 52:29.688
That's impossible.

52:43.910 --> 52:45.579
There's no way that can be true.

52:45.662 --> 52:46.746
Ung?

52:52.377 --> 52:54.087
Why are you here?

52:54.880 --> 52:58.091
I heard that you moved back here.

52:58.967 --> 53:01.428
Is that why
we ran into each other so often?

53:02.012 --> 53:03.680
Oh, did you?

53:06.433 --> 53:07.642
Have you been drinking?

53:07.726 --> 53:09.895
What? Well…

53:11.229 --> 53:12.397
I did.

53:13.356 --> 53:15.901
By the way,
what brings you here at this hour?

53:17.402 --> 53:18.278
I don't know.

53:19.070 --> 53:21.364
I've only realized
how late it was after I got here

53:21.448 --> 53:23.742
so I was thinking of just going home.

53:26.119 --> 53:28.330
If it's not urgent, can we talk next time?

53:28.413 --> 53:30.957
I'm really tired right now.

54:39.150 --> 54:40.652
It's you again.

54:46.032 --> 54:47.283
I must be dreaming again.

54:56.001 --> 54:57.252
I won't fall for it.

55:03.049 --> 55:04.134
Yeon-su.

55:14.269 --> 55:15.770
I'm in so much pain.

55:29.451 --> 55:32.620
I remembered it again.

55:32.704 --> 55:35.832
Are you okay? You seem pretty drunk.

55:37.250 --> 55:38.835
No, I'm fine.

55:42.589 --> 55:43.673
You see…

55:45.425 --> 55:46.259
About last night…

55:48.887 --> 55:52.557
Well, I saw a Thermos bottle at my house.

55:52.640 --> 55:53.933
Is that yours?

55:55.143 --> 55:58.104
I'm relieved he doesn't remember.

55:59.230 --> 56:03.401
Yes. You seemed out of it,
so I left it there.

56:05.111 --> 56:06.446
Really?

56:06.529 --> 56:09.949
Yes. You had taken some pills.
You were in a daze.

56:11.451 --> 56:13.495
Did I fall asleep after you left?

56:14.788 --> 56:15.789
I think so.

56:18.583 --> 56:20.627
Oh, I see.

56:21.503 --> 56:23.379
Did you come here to ask me that?

56:24.798 --> 56:26.174
You could've just called.

56:30.512 --> 56:32.597
I'll keep that memory to myself.

56:33.932 --> 56:35.266
I should head inside.

56:35.975 --> 56:37.102
Bye.

56:37.811 --> 56:39.395
That's how it should be.

56:39.938 --> 56:43.191
Then you can pretend
like you don't remember tomorrow.

56:46.361 --> 56:47.529
It wasn't a dream.

56:52.075 --> 56:53.535
Why are you acting as if it was?

56:58.331 --> 56:59.541
Why are you lying?

57:01.626 --> 57:02.710
Yeon-su.

57:09.968 --> 57:10.969
Yeon-su.

57:28.069 --> 57:29.446
Is this right?

57:33.241 --> 57:35.410
Is it right for us to be like this?

57:46.963 --> 57:49.382
It's us of all people.

57:53.219 --> 57:55.138
Our love wasn't just lukewarm…

57:58.558 --> 58:00.643
and neither was our breakup.

58:02.645 --> 58:04.105
Now that we've reunited,

58:06.107 --> 58:07.734
we can say, "Have you been well?"

58:10.361 --> 58:11.988
"How have you been?"

58:13.573 --> 58:14.991
"Was it tough for you?"

58:16.868 --> 58:19.621
"It was tough for me."
Can't we tell each other these things?

58:23.249 --> 58:24.751
The reason why we broke up…

58:28.630 --> 58:29.756
How have you been?

58:30.673 --> 58:32.217
was because of my pride.

58:32.800 --> 58:34.052
Answer me.

58:35.845 --> 58:36.971
How have you been?

58:37.972 --> 58:39.974
It was my pride that told me

58:42.519 --> 58:44.354
that I could live without you.

58:57.116 --> 59:04.123
PRIDE AND PREJUDICE

59:24.936 --> 59:25.812
EPILOGUE

59:25.895 --> 59:27.564
Drawing is just going to be a hobby.

59:28.231 --> 59:29.107
You know my dream.

59:29.190 --> 59:32.860
It's to bask in the sun during the day
and to lie underneath a lamp at night.

59:33.528 --> 59:35.280
A stressful life is not for me.

59:36.155 --> 59:36.990
One minute.

59:42.161 --> 59:43.496
Did I sound too pathetic?

59:49.794 --> 59:53.131
JOBS FOR DESIGN MAJORS

59:55.717 --> 59:56.718
HOW EASY IS IT TO GET A JOB?

59:56.801 --> 59:58.595
MAKING MONEY THROUGH DRAWING

59:59.971 --> 01:00:02.890
4 MONTHS AFTER THE BREAKUP

01:00:50.730 --> 01:00:55.735
Subtitle translation by: Soo-ji Kim
